    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\nRight now Cython ships wrappers for the C++ standard library atomics API. It would be nice for free-threading support to also have access to C11 atomics, particularly for existing extensions that don't yet compile under C++.\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like.\n\nHave `libc.atomic` wrappers shipped with Cython, like `libcpp.atomic`.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered.\n\nDownstream libraries can wrap the standard library themselves. They can also use C++.\n\n### Additional context\n\nSee https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32889#discussion_r4263601255 for when this came up in NumPy.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
